== E.2 PER-COMPONENT SOURCE EXPRESSIONS (strongest form the bytes support) ==

  out.x (out[0], byte offset +0) = f32( f32( W.x * K ) - S.x )
  out.y (out[1], byte offset +4) = f32( f32( W.y * K ) - S.y )
  out.z (out[2], byte offset +8) = f32( f32( W.z * K ) - S.z )

  where:
    W.x/W.y/W.z = m_kWorld.m_Translate components of the named NiAVObject (engine-space translate, f32)
    K           = (double)(float)0.01 = 0.009999999776482582 (bit pattern 0x3F847AE140000000, qword at 0xa7b360)
    S.x/S.y/S.z = singleton base components (f32 at [S+0]/[S+4]/[S+8])
    S           = { [0xba921c], [0xba9220], [0xba9224] } snapshot at first 0x437F70 call

  GIVEN E.3 (S == {0,0,0} always), the load-bearing reduction (bit-exact under x87 extended precision
  + round-to-nearest for the two f32 narrowings; sign-of-zero preserved):

    out.x = f32(W.x * 0.01f)      out.y = f32(W.y * 0.01f)      out.z = f32(W.z * 0.01f)
    (the multiplications use (double)(float)0.01 in f80, then narrow twice: f32(x*K) then f32(... - 0.0f) == f32(x*K))

  NO axis permutation (component i of source -> component i of out, measured addressing [edx]/[edx+4]/[edx+8] ->
  [eax]/[eax+4]/[eax+8] in order). NO negation. NO offset. ONE multiplicative scale. ONE additive base (=0).

== E.3 S == {0,0,0} — PROOF THAT THE BASE IS THE ZERO VECTOR ==

  MEASURED_QUANTITY: existence of ANY write to 0xba921c/0xba9220/0xba9224 anywhere in the image.
  Method (4 independent write-vector scans, all executed):
    (1) Exact write encodings in .text (A3 imm32 / 89 /r imm32 / C7 05 imm32 imm32 / D9 15 / D9 1D for each of the
        3 addresses): 0 hits.
    (2) imm32 computed bases in [0xba9200,0xba9240] (a base+disp writer would embed a nearby constant):
        0xba920c: 'test byte [0xba920c],1' + 'or dword [0xba920c],1' (flags, stops at 0xba920f);
        0xba9210: 'mov dword [0xba9210], 0xa9c45c' + 'mov dword [0xba9210], eax' (pointer slot, writes 0xba9210..13);
        0xba9218: 'test byte [0xba9218],al' + 'or dword [0xba9218],eax' (flags, writes 0xba9218..1b).
        ALL neighborhood writes STOP AT 0xba921b — none touches the triple.
    (3) Stored pointers to the triple family in ALL non-.text sections (a global pointer variable enabling dynamic
        writes): 0 hits.
    (4) Pointer-passing sites ('push 0xba921c' x5: 0x441040/0x441045 -> callee 0x6C9490; 0x46ab60/0x46ab65 -> same
        pattern; 0x46e7d8/0x46e7e6 -> callees 0x730F90/0x730FB0): all decoded — 0x730F90/0x730FB0 READ the triple into
        a local matrix (rows at this+8/0x14); 0x6C9490 COPIES the triple into its object (+0x3C..0x44, +0x48..0x50).
        All consumers READ; none writes.
    Additionally the triple lives in the .data VIRTUAL-ONLY tail (RVA 0x7A921C - 0x76C000 = 0x3D21C > rawsize 0x34000):
    zero-initialized by the loader, no static initializer bytes exist.
  INDEPENDENT_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH: raw byte scans of the image (documented above), not interpretation.
  WHY_NON_CIRCULAR: the proof is a negative-existence scan over all encoding channels, independent of any report.
